# Client API base URL. Leave empty for same-origin deployments (the default):
# the client then targets the current page's origin (/api), proxied to the
# backend by the Vite dev server in dev and by nginx in production. The
# protocol always follows the current page at runtime (see src/services/
# api-url.ts), so HTTPS deployments never issue mixed content. For a
# cross-origin API, set it to the API's full origin, e.g. https://api.example.com/api
VITE_API_URL=
